"use strict";(self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_package_slips_doc=self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_package_slips_doc||[]).push([[88],{1255(e,i,a){a.r(i),a.d(i,{_pageData:()=>o,default:()=>s});var t=a(641);const o=JSON.parse('{"path":"/woocommerce-package-slips/installation.html","title":"Installation Guide","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{"title":"Installation Guide","description":"Step-by-step instructions for installing and activating the WooCommerce PDF Invoices & Packing Slips plugin."},"git":{},"filePathRelative":"woocommerce-package-slips/installation.md"}'),n={name:"installation.md"},s=(0,a(6262).A)(n,[["render",function(e,i,a,o,n,s){return(0,t.uX)(),(0,t.CE)("div",null,[...i[0]||(i[0]=[(0,t.Fv)('<h1 id="installation-getting-started" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#installation-getting-started"><span>Installation &amp; Getting Started</span></a></h1><p>Getting started with the <strong>PDF Invoices &amp; Packing Slips for WooCommerce</strong> plugin takes only a few minutes. This guide covers how to install the plugin, activate it, and access the configuration menus.</p><hr><h2 id="method-1-wordpress-admin-dashboard-recommended" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#method-1-wordpress-admin-dashboard-recommended"><span>Method 1: WordPress Admin Dashboard (Recommended)</span></a></h2><h3 id="step-1-access-plugin-installation" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#step-1-access-plugin-installation"><span>Step 1: Access Plugin Installation</span></a></h3><ol><li>Log in to your WordPress Admin Panel.</li><li>Navigate to: <strong>Plugins</strong> → <strong>Add New Plugin</strong>.</li><li>Click the <strong>Upload Plugin</strong> button at the top of the page.</li></ol><p><img src="/woocommerce-pdf-invoices-packing-slips/images/woocommerce-package-slips/installation-add-new.webp" alt="Access Plugin Upload"></p><h3 id="step-2-upload-the-plugin" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#step-2-upload-the-plugin"><span>Step 2: Upload the Plugin</span></a></h3><ol><li>Click the <strong>Choose File</strong> button.</li><li>Select the downloaded plugin ZIP file (<code>woo-pdf-invoices-packing-slips.zip</code>).</li><li>Click <strong>Install Now</strong>.</li></ol><p><img src="/woocommerce-pdf-invoices-packing-slips/images/woocommerce-package-slips/installation-upload-plugin.webp" alt="Upload Plugin Zip"></p><h3 id="step-3-activate-the-plugin" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#step-3-activate-the-plugin"><span>Step 3: Activate the Plugin</span></a></h3><ol><li>After successful installation, click the <strong>Activate Plugin</strong> button.</li><li>Wait for the activation confirmation message.</li></ol><p><img src="/woocommerce-pdf-invoices-packing-slips/images/woocommerce-package-slips/installation-activate-plugin.webp" alt="Activate Plugin"></p><hr><h2 id="method-2-ftp-installation-alternative" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#method-2-ftp-installation-alternative"><span>Method 2: FTP Installation (Alternative)</span></a></h2><p>If you prefer to upload files directly to your server or if your admin dashboard file limits prevent uploads:</p><h3 id="step-1-prepare-files" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#step-1-prepare-files"><span>Step 1: Prepare Files</span></a></h3><ol><li>Locate the downloaded plugin ZIP file on your computer.</li><li>Uncompress/Unzip the package.</li><li>Extract the <code>woo-pdf-invoices-packing-slips</code> folder.</li></ol><h3 id="step-2-upload-via-ftp" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#step-2-upload-via-ftp"><span>Step 2: Upload via FTP</span></a></h3><ol><li>Connect to your web hosting server using your preferred FTP/SFTP client.</li><li>Navigate to your WordPress root plugins folder: <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code>.</li><li>Upload the entire extracted <code>woo-pdf-invoices-packing-slips</code> folder.</li></ol><h3 id="step-3-activate" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#step-3-activate"><span>Step 3: Activate</span></a></h3><ol><li>Log in to your WordPress Admin dashboard.</li><li>Go to <strong>Plugins</strong> → <strong>Installed Plugins</strong>.</li><li>Find <strong>Woo PDF Invoices &amp; Packing Slips</strong> in the list and click <strong>Activate</strong>.</li></ol><hr><h2 id="post-installation-checks" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#post-installation-checks"><span>Post-Installation Checks</span></a></h2><p>Before configuring settings or generating invoices, perform the following validation checks:</p><ul><li><strong>Clear Caches:</strong> If you are using any server-side cache, CDN, or WordPress caching plugins (e.g., WP Rocket, W3 Total Cache), clear your cache to make sure new admin scripts load.</li><li><strong>Verify Installation:</strong> Ensure that the plugin appears under your active plugins list and that no script errors are displayed.</li><li><strong>Verify System Paths:</strong> Ensure your server directory <code>/wp-content/uploads/</code> has write permissions enabled (<code>755</code> or <code>777</code>), as the PDF engine uses this path to temporarily write and compile PDF invoice files.</li></ul><hr><h2 id="accessing-the-plugin-menus" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#accessing-the-plugin-menus"><span>Accessing the Plugin Menus</span></a></h2><p>Once activated, the plugin adds two main areas to your WooCommerce admin dashboard.</p><h3 id="_1-the-pdf-invoices-document-portal" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-the-pdf-invoices-document-portal"><span>1. The PDF Invoices Document Portal</span></a></h3><p>To see all generated documents, download archives, or filter invoices by date range:</p><ul><li>Navigate to <strong>WooCommerce</strong> → <strong>PDF Invoices</strong> in the WordPress sidebar.</li><li>Here you can view, filter, and bulk-download generated Invoices, Packing Slips, Proforma Invoices, Credit Notes, and Picking Lists.</li></ul><h3 id="_2-the-configuration-settings" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-the-configuration-settings"><span>2. The Configuration Settings</span></a></h3><p>To configure your document settings, branding, numbering patterns, and templates:</p><ul><li>Navigate to <strong>WooCommerce</strong> → <strong>Settings</strong> → <strong>PDF Invoices</strong> tab.</li><li>This tab is divided into sub-sections: <em>General</em>, <em>Numbering</em>, <em>Appearance</em>, <em>Templates</em>, <em>Checkout</em>, and <em>Export &amp; Reset</em>.</li></ul><hr><h2 id="pre-activation-checklist" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#pre-activation-checklist"><span>Pre-activation Checklist</span></a></h2><p>Before configuring your settings, gather the following details to speed up your setup process:</p><ul><li><strong>Company Details:</strong> Your legal business name, physical street address, and contact information.</li><li><strong>Branding Assets:</strong> A high-resolution copy of your company logo (supported formats: PNG, JPG, or SVG).</li><li><strong>Tax Information:</strong> Your tax office identifier or VAT number.</li><li><strong>Sequence Prefix:</strong> The abbreviation or prefix you want to use for your invoices (e.g., <code>INV-2026-</code>).</li></ul>',39)])])}]])}}]);